# Reviewed exceptions to `ws check-secrets`. One entry per line:
#
#   <path-glob> <rule|*> <regex>
#
# An entry allows a finding when all three hold: the path glob matches the file, the rule matches
# (or is *), and the regex matches in the line of the finding, overlapping the finding's own
# text. Any other finding on the same line stays blocked. Lines starting with # are comments, so
# the reason for an entry goes in a comment above it.
#
# The path glob is relative to the repo root and is matched against the whole path: * and ? stay
# inside one folder, ** crosses folders (docs/** is everything under docs; **/ also matches no
# folder at all). A binary file has no lines to read, so it is a binary-file finding that needs
# an entry; there the regex is matched against the path.
#
# Rules: secret-assignment, token-prefix, url-credentials, io-host, private-ip, home-path,
# real-name, blocked-domain, binary-file. A rule * entry needs a glob that does not cover every
# file.
#
# The check reads this file as staged, not from the work tree: an exception counts once it is
# added to the index, and so it shows up in the diff that is reviewed.

# samples that must trigger each pattern rule
tests/test_secrets.py secret-assignment .*
tests/test_secrets.py url-credentials .*
tests/test_secrets.py io-host .*
tests/test_secrets.py private-ip .*
tests/test_secrets.py home-path .*

# public reference sites cited in the research notes
docs/research/*.md io-host (modelcontextprotocol|snyk)\.io

# local Docker test stacks of the Artemis stress and replica prototypes (throwaway teste/admin users)
projetos/artemis-v2/anexos/estresse/compose.yml secret-assignment PASSWOR[D]: (teste|admin)\b
projetos/artemis-v2/anexos/estresse/compose.yml url-credentials :/[/](teste:teste|admin:admin)@
projetos/artemis-v2/anexos/replica/README.md secret-assignment PASSWOR[D]=teste\b
projetos/artemis-v2/anexos/replica/test_routing.py url-credentials :/[/]teste:teste@

# connection-string placeholders, not credentials
skills/**/*.md url-credentials :/[/]<[\w-]+>:<[\w-]+>@

# front-end source paths of the portal (features/general/home/...), not a user home folder
projetos/reestrutura-whitelabel/** home-path general/home/[\w.-]*

# prose: "token" as a design token or an access-token claim, "secret" as a fallback
projetos/reestrutura-whitelabel/anexos/ilustracoes/ilustracoes.mjs secret-assignment um toke[n]: accent
projetos/reestrutura-whitelabel/tarefas/27-organizacao-e-cliente.md secret-assignment ao toke[n]: claims
projetos/reestrutura-whitelabel/tarefas/29-seguranca-infra.md secret-assignment o secre[t]: faltando
